# ARC-27: allow podman to SIGTERM the shared-rootless-netns pasta holder.
#
# Podman reclaims the shared rootless netns by signaling its helper
# (pasta) with SIGTERM. Ubuntu/Debian ship an AppArmor profile for
# pasta in enforce mode whose signal rules predate that handoff, so
# the profile denies "signal (receive) signal=term peer=podman" and
# every shared-netns operation fails with podman's cryptic:
#
#   Error: rootless netns: kill network process: permission denied
#
# This one rule keeps the profile ENFORCED (the signal is the only
# thing being widened) instead of falling back to `aa-complain`, which
# logs every pasta denial and is the whole-profile answer.
#
# Apply: see README.md in this directory.

signal (receive) set=(term) peer=podman,
